### Atlas Liquidity Platform — Layer 1 API examples
#
# Install the "REST Client" VS Code extension (humao.rest-client), then click
# the "Send Request" link that appears above each request.
#
# Why this file is checked into the repo rather than living in Postman:
# it is versioned with the code, it reviews in a pull request, and a new
# engineer can exercise the API within a minute of cloning. Postman
# collections drift; this does not.

@host = http://localhost:8081

### List all settlement accounts
GET {{host}}/api/v1/accounts
Accept: application/json

### Filter by currency
GET {{host}}/api/v1/accounts?currency=USD
Accept: application/json

### Filter by jurisdiction (drives data residency from Layer 11)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/accounts?jurisdiction=EU
Accept: application/json

### Fetch a single account
GET {{host}}/api/v1/accounts/ACC-EU-0001
Accept: application/json

### 404 — returns an RFC 7807 problem detail, not an HTML error page
GET {{host}}/api/v1/accounts/ACC-DOES-NOT-EXIST
Accept: application/json

### 400 — unknown jurisdiction, with an actionable message
GET {{host}}/api/v1/accounts?jurisdiction=ATLANTIS
Accept: application/json

### Supply your own correlation id — check it comes back in the response header
#   and appears in the service's console log for this request
GET {{host}}/api/v1/accounts
X-Correlation-Id: dinesh-manual-test-001
Accept: application/json

### Health — this is the endpoint Kubernetes probes in Layer 10
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

### Liveness probe
GET {{host}}/actuator/health/liveness

### Readiness probe
GET {{host}}/actuator/health/readiness

### Build and app info
GET {{host}}/actuator/info

### Metrics index (Prometheus scrapes /actuator/prometheus from Layer 10)
GET {{host}}/actuator/metrics
